1
00:01:47,120 --> 00:01:48,879
It was before I went to prison

2
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:51,519
that I found out my daughter was pregnant.

3
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,000
She originally wanted to have an abortion.

4
00:01:54,799 --> 00:01:56,560
But the doctor said she was too weak

5
00:01:57,159 --> 00:01:58,480
and an abortion was too dangerous.

6
00:01:58,640 --> 00:02:00,560
So she ended up having the baby.

7
00:02:01,519 --> 00:02:03,799
My wife was afraid that keeping the baby

8
00:02:03,879 --> 00:02:05,920
would ruin our daughter's reputation.

9
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:07,879
So she lied to my daughter, saying

10
00:02:08,199 --> 00:02:10,479
the baby died at birth.

11
00:02:11,240 --> 00:02:12,439
My poor daughter...

12
00:02:12,599 --> 00:02:13,879
She hadn't even finished her confinement

13
00:02:14,159 --> 00:02:15,400
before she left our hometown.

14
00:02:16,199 --> 00:02:17,520
We haven't heard from her since.

15
00:02:18,719 --> 00:02:23,280
My wife raised the child for three years,

16
00:02:23,879 --> 00:02:25,000
then she passed away from illness, too.

17
00:02:26,639 --> 00:02:28,960
Then as for the child,

18
00:02:31,319 --> 00:02:32,520
who is taking care of him now?

19
00:02:33,439 --> 00:02:35,919
He is living with his uncle.

20
00:02:36,199 --> 00:02:39,280
But how could his uncle afford to raise a child?

21
00:02:39,719 --> 00:02:41,960
It was the lawyer from the second-instance trial

22
00:02:42,039 --> 00:02:44,280
who kept sending money to his uncle's family.

23
00:02:44,719 --> 00:02:47,240
The young lawyer was just a stranger.

24
00:02:47,479 --> 00:02:49,879
Why would he help raise our grandson for nothing?

25
00:02:50,919 --> 00:02:53,360
It's simply because you were a senior judge.

26
00:02:54,120 --> 00:02:55,280
Now that you aren't anymore,

27
00:02:55,919 --> 00:02:57,280
will he still send money?

28
00:02:58,120 --> 00:02:59,439
Who was the lawyer

29
00:03:01,199 --> 00:03:02,039
from the second-instance trial?

30
00:03:35,319 --> 00:03:37,240
I'm really sorry, Mr. Yu.

31
00:03:38,159 --> 00:03:39,280
Attorney Zhao is really busy.

32
00:03:39,560 --> 00:03:40,639
I'll remind him again.

33
00:03:40,639 --> 00:03:41,960
It's okay. No rush.

34
00:03:42,159 --> 00:03:43,000
Please have a seat.

35
00:03:53,879 --> 00:03:54,599
Hello.

36
00:03:56,319 --> 00:03:57,879
We've been waiting for over three hours.

37
00:04:01,400 --> 00:04:02,080
Okay.

38
00:04:05,879 --> 00:04:07,400
Sorry to keep you waiting, Mr. Yu.

39
00:04:07,680 --> 00:04:08,520
Follow me.

40
00:04:08,840 --> 00:04:10,000
Okay, thank you.

41
00:04:15,879 --> 00:04:16,680
Right this way.

42
00:04:18,519 --> 00:04:20,120
Mr. Zhao, he's here.

43
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:24,639
Mr. Zhao.

44
00:04:25,680 --> 00:04:26,680
He's arrived.

45
00:04:30,519 --> 00:04:32,000
Would you two like something to drink?

46
00:04:35,680 --> 00:04:36,319
No, thanks.

47
00:04:41,680 --> 00:04:43,160
He fell asleep again.

48
00:04:46,600 --> 00:04:48,720
First time waiting for a lawyer, Judge Yu?

49
00:04:48,720 --> 00:04:49,480
I apologize.

50
00:04:49,879 --> 00:04:51,079
Hello, Yu Songfan.

51
00:04:51,319 --> 00:04:52,720
Give me a second.

52
00:04:55,759 --> 00:04:57,839
This is your math test.

53
00:04:58,839 --> 00:05:00,480
And this is my little security camera.

54
00:05:01,399 --> 00:05:03,199
And you taking videos for me here...

55
00:05:03,800 --> 00:05:06,160
Actually, doing all these strange things...

56
00:05:07,720 --> 00:05:08,959
What was your intention?

57
00:05:16,360 --> 00:05:18,319
Are you sure you don't need me to take care of her for you?

58
00:05:19,399 --> 00:05:20,839
This is between her and me.

59
00:05:20,839 --> 00:05:22,199
I'll handle it myself.

60
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:23,720
All right.

61
00:05:28,319 --> 00:05:29,639
I've met Yang Cheng.

62
00:05:30,560 --> 00:05:32,720
He told me everything.

63
00:05:34,839 --> 00:05:35,720
It's been eight years.

64
00:05:37,399 --> 00:05:39,439
Why did you wait until today to come to me?

65
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:42,199
Every time I play with this thing,

66
00:05:43,519 --> 00:05:44,680
it always reminds me of you.

67
00:05:47,120 --> 00:05:48,680
I think you two are very similar.

68
00:05:50,240 --> 00:05:52,399
No matter how hard I squeeze, it won't break.

69
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:56,639
See? Doesn't it look like you?

70
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:02,160
I'm not like your foolish colleagues.

71
00:06:02,720 --> 00:06:05,279
I know that beneath your nice-guy exterior,

72
00:06:05,279 --> 00:06:07,519
you are an incredibly smart man.

73
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:11,360
So I couldn't let you in on my plans.

74
00:06:11,720 --> 00:06:13,639
Or you would've escaped my trap long ago.

75
00:06:13,920 --> 00:06:15,959
But despite all my calculations,

76
00:06:17,160 --> 00:06:20,040
I never figured you'd get Alzheimer's.

77
00:06:21,600 --> 00:06:23,079
And that you'd get reported.

78
00:06:26,160 --> 00:06:27,279
But this is actually perfect.

79
00:06:27,839 --> 00:06:29,360
What do you mean, perfect?

80
00:06:38,120 --> 00:06:39,879
So you just wanted to tell me

81
00:06:39,879 --> 00:06:42,959
that your adoption of Yang Awu is legal?

82
00:06:43,240 --> 00:06:44,879
I've raised him for eight years.

83
00:06:46,079 --> 00:06:47,360
I care about him deeply.

84
00:06:47,600 --> 00:06:49,560
And he's willing to call me "Dad."

85
00:06:50,519 --> 00:06:52,360
I find it very heartwarming and cozy.

86
00:06:54,279 --> 00:06:55,199
I don't have children of my own.

87
00:06:55,839 --> 00:06:57,160
So I will definitely treat him well.

88
00:06:57,160 --> 00:06:57,920
You can rest assured.

89
00:06:57,920 --> 00:06:59,079
You adopted him,

90
00:07:00,199 --> 00:07:02,000
even though you clearly know he's...

91
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:04,360
I know he's your son's own flesh and blood.

92
00:07:06,079 --> 00:07:07,319
But, Mr. Yu,

93
00:07:08,040 --> 00:07:09,680
do you currently

94
00:07:11,399 --> 00:07:12,519
dare to acknowledge him?

95
00:07:14,480 --> 00:07:16,879
Dare to take the massive secret

96
00:07:16,879 --> 00:07:20,360
you've kept for your precious son so long

97
00:07:21,199 --> 00:07:22,240
and reveal it to the public?

98
00:07:23,319 --> 00:07:24,639
Or, like me,

99
00:07:25,360 --> 00:07:28,639
go and get a registered adoption certificate.

100
00:07:31,720 --> 00:07:33,000
Do you dare?

101
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:40,000
As for Ah Wu,

102
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:42,319
he's such a sensible and well-behaved kid.

103
00:07:42,319 --> 00:07:44,000
I'm very fond of him.

104
00:07:44,160 --> 00:07:46,000
So I'm planning to send him abroad

105
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:47,040
for further studies.

106
00:07:47,120 --> 00:07:49,839
But when he returns from his studies,

107
00:07:50,920 --> 00:07:52,519
I wonder if your condition, Mr. Yu,

108
00:07:52,519 --> 00:07:53,800
will have worsened so much

109
00:07:54,519 --> 00:07:56,639
that you won't remember having a grandson.

110
00:07:59,319 --> 00:08:00,240
Mr. Zhao.

111
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:02,040
I don't recall ever meeting you.

112
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:04,360
And we don't know each other.

113
00:08:04,600 --> 00:08:06,480
Have I ever hurt your parents,

114
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:08,839
relatives, friends, or wife?

115
00:08:09,360 --> 00:08:10,040
Have I?

116
00:08:10,519 --> 00:08:11,639
Otherwise, why would you

117
00:08:11,639 --> 00:08:13,439
take this attitude and approach

118
00:08:13,439 --> 00:08:14,560
in dealing with me?

119
00:08:14,879 --> 00:08:16,879
Is there anything we can't

120
00:08:16,879 --> 00:08:18,720
discuss openly and aboveboard?

121
00:08:19,519 --> 00:08:21,240
Open and aboveboard.

122
00:08:21,680 --> 00:08:22,319
Right.

123
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:24,040
In the Palace of Heavenly Purity,

124
00:08:24,040 --> 00:08:27,079
there's an "Open and Aboveboard" plaque.

125
00:08:28,439 --> 00:08:29,720
Do you know what it's used for?

126
00:08:30,360 --> 00:08:32,159
Behind that plaque is a small box

127
00:08:32,159 --> 00:08:33,519
called the Succession Box.

128
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:36,080
Inside is the name of the Crown Prince.

129
00:08:36,080 --> 00:08:37,200
Tell me, the emperor's sons,

130
00:08:37,200 --> 00:08:38,639
seeing "Open and Aboveboard" every day...

131
00:08:38,639 --> 00:08:39,639
I have no idea

132
00:08:39,639 --> 00:08:40,759
what this history you're talking about

133
00:08:40,759 --> 00:08:42,399
has to do with this matter.

134
00:08:42,720 --> 00:08:44,480
I don't want to hear any more of your nonsense.

135
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:46,240
I want to see my grandson right now.

136
00:08:47,360 --> 00:08:48,240
Can I?

137
00:08:54,519 --> 00:08:55,919
I'll let that slide this once.

138
00:09:02,720 --> 00:09:05,639
I have an intermediate court case opening

139
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:07,840
next week. The presiding judge is Ou Qi.

140
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:10,360
But as for this case,

141
00:09:10,600 --> 00:09:13,240
if it could be postponed to next month,

142
00:09:13,240 --> 00:09:14,279
that would be fantastic.

143
00:09:14,559 --> 00:09:16,120
So you're meeting me just to

144
00:09:16,240 --> 00:09:18,519
use my grandson to blackmail me into it?

145
00:09:18,519 --> 00:09:19,200
Is that it?

146
00:09:19,320 --> 00:09:20,320
No, no, no.

147
00:09:21,440 --> 00:09:23,039
I'm just staring at that

148
00:09:23,039 --> 00:09:24,919
"Open and Aboveboard" plaque.

149
00:09:29,720 --> 00:09:30,919
Also, how can I be sure

150
00:09:30,919 --> 00:09:32,000
that the child you adopted

151
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:33,279
is really my son's?

152
00:09:35,919 --> 00:09:36,720
Brilliant.

153
00:09:45,840 --> 00:09:47,240
The massage parlor

154
00:09:47,240 --> 00:09:49,159
is just a small business of mine.

155
00:09:49,600 --> 00:09:50,639
I didn't let you go there for nothing.

156
00:09:51,159 --> 00:09:51,600
I collected some of

157
00:09:51,600 --> 00:09:52,440
your DNA samples

158
00:09:52,440 --> 00:09:53,519
and ran a paternity test.

159
00:09:54,159 --> 00:09:54,799
No rush.

160
00:09:55,320 --> 00:09:57,320
Take it home and look it over thoroughly.

161
00:09:58,240 --> 00:10:00,000
We're both legal professionals.

162
00:10:00,840 --> 00:10:02,279
Neither of us can make

163
00:10:02,279 --> 00:10:04,840
baseless claims without evidence,

164
00:10:05,080 --> 00:10:05,639
right?

165
00:10:08,919 --> 00:10:09,759
Also,

166
00:10:14,559 --> 00:10:15,639
a little gift.

167
00:10:23,039 --> 00:10:24,159
Bye.

168
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:30,159
Thank you. Say thank you.

169
00:11:30,440 --> 00:11:31,200
Thank you.

170
00:12:46,759 --> 00:12:47,559
Who is it?

171
00:12:47,559 --> 00:12:48,919
Do you know what time it is?

172
00:12:49,200 --> 00:12:50,519
Old Yu! It's Old Ou.

173
00:12:50,960 --> 00:12:51,960
Old Yu.

174
00:12:57,559 --> 00:12:59,679
I don't think I can be alone right now.

175
00:13:06,559 --> 00:13:07,480
Thank you. Thank you.

176
00:13:07,480 --> 00:13:08,600
Come on, let's go inside.

177
00:13:08,600 --> 00:13:09,279
Okay.

178
00:13:12,360 --> 00:13:13,960
So, we won the lawsuit.

179
00:13:14,120 --> 00:13:15,440
It was Lawyer Ding here

180
00:13:15,559 --> 00:13:17,240
who won this case for us.

181
00:13:17,360 --> 00:13:18,200
So, you see,

182
00:13:18,600 --> 00:13:20,200
about the balance of the legal fees,

183
00:13:20,200 --> 00:13:21,200
can we settle it now?

184
00:13:23,200 --> 00:13:24,080
I beg to differ.

185
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:26,279
For this debt dispute of mine,

186
00:13:26,440 --> 00:13:28,639
I only found out on the day of the trial

187
00:13:28,919 --> 00:13:30,720
that I just needed to provide two pages

188
00:13:31,159 --> 00:13:33,519
and I'd naturally win the case.

189
00:13:33,759 --> 00:13:34,639
Two pages.

190
00:13:37,440 --> 00:13:39,840
Raising a statute of limitations defense.

191
00:13:41,480 --> 00:13:42,840
No matter how you spin it,

192
00:13:42,840 --> 00:13:45,360
it's still just a piece of paper!

193
00:13:45,799 --> 00:13:46,600
You can't just

194
00:13:46,600 --> 00:13:48,519
charge me 30,000 yuan in legal fees!

195
00:13:50,080 --> 00:13:51,559
I mean, do you lawyers

196
00:13:51,559 --> 00:13:53,960
take us newly rich people

197
00:13:53,960 --> 00:13:55,159
for fools?

198
00:13:55,480 --> 00:13:57,000
You just ran some errands for me,

199
00:13:57,039 --> 00:13:58,879
submitted a few papers to the court,

200
00:13:58,960 --> 00:14:00,440
and now you're demanding money.

201
00:14:00,679 --> 00:14:02,240
Aren't you ripping me off a bit?

202
00:14:02,360 --> 00:14:03,159
Look,

203
00:14:03,480 --> 00:14:05,480
our firm put in the work for this.

204
00:14:05,799 --> 00:14:08,000
We got it after careful investigation.

205
00:14:08,039 --> 00:14:10,399
Is there something you're unsatisfied with?

206
00:14:12,679 --> 00:14:13,600
I'm sorry, boss.

207
00:14:14,120 --> 00:14:15,399
I really need the money,

208
00:14:15,399 --> 00:14:16,080
but...

209
00:14:17,360 --> 00:14:18,279
I'm leaving.

210
00:14:21,080 --> 00:14:21,919
Hold on a second.

211
00:14:23,039 --> 00:14:24,120
What are you doing?

212
00:14:25,039 --> 00:14:26,639
It's not your first time with such people.

213
00:14:26,840 --> 00:14:28,600
There's still no news on the drug dealer's case.

214
00:14:29,399 --> 00:14:30,399
It's not just about the drug dealer.

215
00:14:30,559 --> 00:14:31,679
That case is directly tied to

216
00:14:31,679 --> 00:14:32,440
whether we win or lose Zhang Lin's case.

217
00:14:32,440 --> 00:14:33,480
They just told us to wait for an email.

218
00:14:33,879 --> 00:14:35,080
Who knows how long that'll take.

219
00:14:35,159 --> 00:14:36,440
Are you trying to drive yourself crazy?

220
00:14:36,639 --> 00:14:37,639
Or go down with them?

221
00:14:38,440 --> 00:14:40,080
Your body is here, but your mind isn't.

222
00:14:40,320 --> 00:14:41,799
Tell you what, take three days off.

223
00:14:42,200 --> 00:14:43,000
Clear your head.

224
00:14:43,440 --> 00:14:44,440
You don't have to.

225
00:14:44,480 --> 00:14:45,960
I know how busy the firm has been lately.

226
00:14:46,320 --> 00:14:47,919
The world keeps turning without you.

227
00:14:48,240 --> 00:14:49,120
Go, go on.

228
00:14:52,639 --> 00:14:54,960
To catch criminal suspects, police officers

229
00:14:55,279 --> 00:14:57,039
will risk their own lives.

230
00:14:57,759 --> 00:14:58,679
But what about us lawyers?

231
00:14:59,360 --> 00:15:02,440
We rack our brains to help the suspects.

232
00:15:02,639 --> 00:15:03,919
So on the surface,

233
00:15:03,919 --> 00:15:06,799
these two professions seem incompatible.

234
00:15:06,960 --> 00:15:09,080
So it's hard for us to get along.

235
00:15:10,039 --> 00:15:12,120
In truth, we are each just

236
00:15:12,120 --> 00:15:15,000
serving the country and the people.

237
00:15:15,919 --> 00:15:17,240
Zhao Yijie is so young.

238
00:15:17,240 --> 00:15:19,960
Catching criminal suspects is the duty

239
00:15:20,159 --> 00:15:21,960
the law assigns to you detectives.

240
00:15:22,240 --> 00:15:23,960
And defending criminal suspects

241
00:15:24,720 --> 00:15:26,000
is also the duty

242
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:28,200
the law assigns to us lawyers.

243
00:15:29,279 --> 00:15:30,440
Let me first ask you all

244
00:15:30,440 --> 00:15:31,600
a very simple question.

245
00:15:32,080 --> 00:15:32,960
Under our Criminal Law...

246
00:15:32,960 --> 00:15:33,919
What have you been up to lately?

247
00:15:34,279 --> 00:15:35,159
Don't ask.

248
00:15:35,519 --> 00:15:37,440
An armed robbery from four years ago.

249
00:15:37,960 --> 00:15:40,639
Brought the suspect over from Rongshan.

250
00:15:40,879 --> 00:15:42,320
We've interrogated him non-stop for days.

251
00:15:42,320 --> 00:15:43,200
Tell me,

252
00:15:43,840 --> 00:15:44,759
for such a simple question,

253
00:15:44,759 --> 00:15:46,120
don't look it up on your phones.

254
00:15:47,679 --> 00:15:49,000
Which six types? Come on!

255
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:50,399
Meth.

256
00:15:51,720 --> 00:15:52,759
Marijuana.

257
00:15:53,320 --> 00:15:54,519
Cocaine, heroin.

258
00:15:55,080 --> 00:15:55,840
Heroin.

259
00:15:56,679 --> 00:15:57,639
Meth.

260
00:15:58,120 --> 00:15:58,840
And what else?

261
00:15:58,840 --> 00:15:59,559
Cocaine.

262
00:15:59,559 --> 00:16:00,679
Cocaine, morphine.

263
00:16:00,679 --> 00:16:01,600
One more! Hurry!

264
00:16:01,600 --> 00:16:02,720
Opium.

265
00:16:03,759 --> 00:16:04,559
Right.

266
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:05,679
Six types.

267
00:16:05,919 --> 00:16:06,600
Good.

268
00:16:07,759 --> 00:16:09,360
But after Article 357,

269
00:16:09,360 --> 00:16:10,639
there is another half-sentence:

270
00:16:11,320 --> 00:16:14,320
"and other state-regulated

271
00:16:14,320 --> 00:16:17,120
addictive narcotic

272
00:16:17,120 --> 00:16:19,360
and psychotropic substances."

273
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:23,840
The Criminal Law defines what drugs are.

274
00:16:23,960 --> 00:16:25,440
But in actual enforcement,

275
00:16:26,480 --> 00:16:28,519
the scope of such controlled substances

276
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:30,639
is set by the Ministry of Public Security.

277
00:16:31,519 --> 00:16:32,600
So here comes the question.

278
00:16:33,080 --> 00:16:35,919
Do Ministry rules equal state regulations?

279
00:16:37,399 --> 00:16:38,159
A department's regulations,

280
00:16:38,159 --> 00:16:38,759
are they?

281
00:16:38,919 --> 00:16:39,639
Equivalent.

282
00:16:39,919 --> 00:16:40,919
Are they equivalent? Think again.

283
00:16:41,639 --> 00:16:43,440
No, no, no, no.

284
00:16:45,120 --> 00:16:46,200
Not equivalent.

285
00:16:46,440 --> 00:16:47,279
What are they called?

286
00:16:47,759 --> 00:16:49,919
They are called departmental rules.

287
00:16:50,279 --> 00:16:52,519
So, in my personal opinion,

288
00:16:52,600 --> 00:16:53,440
I believe

289
00:16:54,679 --> 00:16:55,799
that for a period of time,

290
00:16:56,080 --> 00:16:58,279
most cases that treat Ministry-regulated

291
00:16:58,279 --> 00:16:59,919
narcotic and psychotropic substances

292
00:17:00,200 --> 00:17:02,919
as drug-related offenses

293
00:17:03,440 --> 00:17:07,440
clearly violated the legality principle.

294
00:17:09,200 --> 00:17:10,079
Clearly,

295
00:17:10,079 --> 00:17:11,200
we knowingly break the law.

296
00:17:11,759 --> 00:17:12,640
But that's not exactly right.

297
00:17:12,640 --> 00:17:14,559
That puts us lawyers in a tough spot.

298
00:17:15,039 --> 00:17:16,000
Sometimes,

299
00:17:16,200 --> 00:17:17,880
we even feel completely powerless.

300
00:17:18,240 --> 00:17:20,680
We also feel for all you detectives here,

301
00:17:20,759 --> 00:17:23,119
for your efforts in catching suspects,

302
00:17:23,400 --> 00:17:24,400
and even the sacrifices you make.

303
00:17:25,359 --> 00:17:26,640
Just like you,

304
00:17:26,960 --> 00:17:27,839
we all hope

305
00:17:27,839 --> 00:17:29,960
those drug dealers burn in hell.

306
00:17:30,480 --> 00:17:32,400
However, from my professional perspective,

307
00:17:34,200 --> 00:17:37,920
our legal system progresses too slowly.

308
00:17:38,119 --> 00:17:40,599
No one likes someone who's always finding fault.

309
00:17:40,599 --> 00:17:41,279
No one.

310
00:17:41,279 --> 00:17:42,160
I don't like them either.

311
00:17:42,160 --> 00:17:43,480
But the progress of the law

312
00:17:43,559 --> 00:17:44,839
and the oversight of power

313
00:17:44,960 --> 00:17:47,200
rely exactly on us troublemakers,

314
00:17:47,359 --> 00:17:48,559
these annoying people.

315
00:17:48,839 --> 00:17:50,240
Because only when contrarians

316
00:17:50,240 --> 00:17:51,279
continue to exist,

317
00:17:51,440 --> 00:17:53,079
in the long run,

318
00:17:53,440 --> 00:17:56,200
can our legal system truly be perfected.

319
00:17:56,920 --> 00:17:58,319
Only then can we better protect

320
00:17:58,319 --> 00:17:59,920
the rights and interests of everyone here.

321
00:18:00,559 --> 00:18:01,440
So I believe

322
00:18:01,720 --> 00:18:03,039
a fair, just,

323
00:18:03,359 --> 00:18:04,880
safe, and harmonious society

324
00:18:05,640 --> 00:18:07,599
cannot exist without you detectives here,

325
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:10,160
nor can it exist without us lawyers.

326
00:18:10,440 --> 00:18:12,680
It's precisely because we are so different,

327
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:15,599
yet so equally dedicated to our duties,

328
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:19,759
that people can live in peace every day.

329
00:18:21,160 --> 00:18:21,920
So,

330
00:18:23,920 --> 00:18:24,759
thank you.

331
00:19:12,720 --> 00:19:13,720
I still remember Old Ding...

332
00:19:13,799 --> 00:19:14,799
turning around back then.

333
00:19:15,240 --> 00:19:16,160
He didn't even do a thing.

334
00:19:16,839 --> 00:19:18,119
He just stared at the drug dealer,

335
00:19:18,680 --> 00:19:20,319
and the punk pissed his pants!

336
00:19:28,480 --> 00:19:29,319
My daughter's back.

337
00:19:29,759 --> 00:19:30,480
Playing cards, huh?

338
00:19:30,839 --> 00:19:32,279
Ding Ning, come here.

339
00:19:32,839 --> 00:19:33,880
Come help me out.

340
00:19:35,839 --> 00:19:36,799
Things were different back then.

341
00:19:37,079 --> 00:19:38,200
We're about to eat.

342
00:19:38,680 --> 00:19:39,839
Take this inside.

343
00:19:40,960 --> 00:19:41,640
Ding Ning.

344
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:44,359
Is work going well lately?

345
00:19:45,240 --> 00:19:46,200
Your Uncle Wang's son

346
00:19:46,200 --> 00:19:48,279
works in HR at a big company.

347
00:19:48,519 --> 00:19:50,480
I told him about your situation.

348
00:19:50,519 --> 00:19:51,359
He said

349
00:19:51,480 --> 00:19:53,079
he wants you to be their legal counsel.

350
00:19:53,279 --> 00:19:54,920
Your monthly pay could be this much.

351
00:19:58,519 --> 00:20:00,279
Okay, I'll think about it.

352
00:20:00,319 --> 00:20:02,160
Stop being so absent-minded.

353
00:20:02,160 --> 00:20:03,000
Last time I brought this up,

354
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:03,960
you also said you'd think about it.

355
00:20:04,160 --> 00:20:05,319
No, today you have to...

356
00:20:05,319 --> 00:20:06,000
Ding Ning!

357
00:20:06,920 --> 00:20:07,759
Come give me a hand!

358
00:20:10,119 --> 00:20:11,119
I'll go help out.

359
00:20:14,319 --> 00:20:16,440
Take it slow. Pushing her won't work.

360
00:20:30,640 --> 00:20:31,400
It worked!

361
00:20:31,759 --> 00:20:33,119
My client's life has been saved.

362
00:20:33,279 --> 00:20:34,279
That wasn't easy.

363
00:20:36,759 --> 00:20:37,480
Hello, Lawyer Ding?

364
00:20:37,759 --> 00:20:39,119
Thank you so much.

365
00:20:39,400 --> 00:20:40,319
As soon as I got the email,

366
00:20:40,319 --> 00:20:41,720
I called you right back.

367
00:20:42,160 --> 00:20:44,599
Whether he is the actual ringleader

368
00:20:44,599 --> 00:20:45,720
will be reinvestigated.

369
00:20:46,160 --> 00:20:47,400
No one expected

370
00:20:47,599 --> 00:20:48,799
that I could help a drug dealer

371
00:20:48,799 --> 00:20:50,440
save his life at the last minute.

372
00:20:52,559 --> 00:20:52,960
Hello?

373
00:20:53,279 --> 00:20:54,240
Hello, Lawyer Ding?

374
00:20:54,880 --> 00:20:55,559
Can you hear me?

375
00:21:03,799 --> 00:21:04,519
Hello?

376
00:21:05,720 --> 00:21:07,240
Anyway, thanks for your advice.

377
00:21:08,720 --> 00:21:09,599
Thank you.

378
00:21:10,880 --> 00:21:11,640
Okay.

379
00:21:13,240 --> 00:21:13,960
I got it.

380
00:21:13,960 --> 00:21:14,839
Ding Ning.

381
00:21:15,200 --> 00:21:16,359
Let's eat first. Come on.

382
00:21:17,480 --> 00:21:18,279
Okay, it's nothing.

383
00:21:21,480 --> 00:21:22,000
Try this.

384
00:21:30,200 --> 00:21:32,559
Dad, that call just now was...

385
00:21:32,559 --> 00:21:34,799
Eat. Let's not talk about it.

386
00:21:35,559 --> 00:21:37,119
I don't take those kinds of cases. Actually...

387
00:21:37,119 --> 00:21:38,240
Um, Ding Ning,

388
00:21:39,119 --> 00:21:40,000
try this dish.

389
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:41,000
I think it's a bit bland.

390
00:21:41,240 --> 00:21:43,160
Could you get me some salt and pepper?

391
00:21:43,920 --> 00:21:45,680
It's just a related case.

392
00:21:45,920 --> 00:21:47,920
A death penalty review for a drug dealer.

393
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:49,839
I just offered some ideas.

394
00:21:49,920 --> 00:21:50,680
I wasn't trying to help him.

395
00:21:50,680 --> 00:21:51,720
Why is nobody eating?

396
00:21:52,680 --> 00:21:53,920
Eat. Let's not talk about it.

397
00:21:55,480 --> 00:21:56,200
By the way, Dad,

398
00:21:56,640 --> 00:21:57,960
I went to the narcotics squad this morning

399
00:21:57,960 --> 00:21:59,359
and attended a lawyer's lecture.

400
00:21:59,640 --> 00:22:00,759
Being a police officer nowadays

401
00:22:00,759 --> 00:22:01,920
means you should keep up with the times.

402
00:22:02,200 --> 00:22:04,400
You need to be more flexible about things.

403
00:22:07,240 --> 00:22:08,680
You're not a narcotics cop.

404
00:22:09,480 --> 00:22:10,640
Why are you attending their lectures?

405
00:22:17,440 --> 00:22:18,559
You helped a drug dealer

406
00:22:20,519 --> 00:22:21,880
and even asked Fan Dong for help?

407
00:22:22,400 --> 00:22:23,759
I didn't, Mom.

408
00:22:23,759 --> 00:22:26,200
Ding Ning, what's wrong with you?

409
00:22:29,960 --> 00:22:30,680
I...

410
00:22:31,720 --> 00:22:33,079
Uncle Wang was blinded

411
00:22:33,240 --> 00:22:35,920
while catching drug dealers back then!

412
00:22:37,680 --> 00:22:38,400
Stop talking.

413
00:22:38,400 --> 00:22:39,200
Eat the fish first.

414
00:22:41,160 --> 00:22:41,519
Mom...

415
00:22:41,519 --> 00:22:42,599
And Fan Dong's younger brother,

416
00:22:45,519 --> 00:22:46,920
all these buddies of your dad's...

417
00:22:47,039 --> 00:22:48,400
Why do they gather every day?

418
00:22:48,599 --> 00:22:49,720
Who are they mourning?

419
00:22:50,319 --> 00:22:51,839
How did Fan Dong lose his father?

420
00:22:52,240 --> 00:22:53,680
Can you really say you don't know?

421
00:22:56,759 --> 00:23:00,160
Mom, every case is different.

422
00:23:00,519 --> 00:23:02,319
And the specific circumstances of each client

423
00:23:02,319 --> 00:23:03,240
are also different.

424
00:23:03,759 --> 00:23:04,960
I'm a lawyer.

425
00:23:05,160 --> 00:23:06,079
There are many things I have no choice...

426
00:23:06,079 --> 00:23:07,400
I said,

427
00:23:09,119 --> 00:23:10,000
eat!

428
00:23:10,599 --> 00:23:11,400
Lao Ding, don't get worked up.

429
00:23:11,400 --> 00:23:11,839
Lao Ding?

430
00:23:12,119 --> 00:23:12,680
Lao Ding!

431
00:23:13,079 --> 00:23:13,799
Lao Ding! Lao Ding! Lao Ding!

432
00:23:13,839 --> 00:23:15,000
Lao Ding, what's wrong? Lao Ding!

433
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:15,759
Lao Ding!

434
00:23:30,039 --> 00:23:30,720
Old Yu

435
00:23:37,440 --> 00:23:38,240
Lawyer Zhao

436
00:23:38,720 --> 00:23:40,480
Why haven't you been answering my calls?

437
00:23:42,960 --> 00:23:44,119
I just...

438
00:23:45,119 --> 00:23:46,880
I just got tired of waiting for judges.

439
00:23:47,759 --> 00:23:49,200
So I wanted a judge to wait for me.

440
00:23:52,640 --> 00:23:55,519
You wanted to secretly delay the hearing.

441
00:23:55,519 --> 00:23:56,240
I made it happen.

442
00:23:58,720 --> 00:23:59,599
So it was you.

443
00:24:01,160 --> 00:24:02,240
I was wondering how

444
00:24:02,240 --> 00:24:04,279
my wish suddenly came true.

445
00:24:04,799 --> 00:24:05,920
I wanted it pushed to next month,

446
00:24:05,920 --> 00:24:07,000
and it got pushed to next month.

447
00:24:08,680 --> 00:24:10,039
However,

448
00:24:11,559 --> 00:24:13,920
this is judicial interference, isn't it?

449
00:24:14,920 --> 00:24:16,920
That's a very serious violation.

450
00:24:17,119 --> 00:24:18,200
And Old Ou,

451
00:24:18,960 --> 00:24:20,559
judge at the Intermediate People's Court.

452
00:24:21,119 --> 00:24:22,440
That good friend of yours.

453
00:24:23,480 --> 00:24:25,400
He knows nothing about our arrangement.

454
00:24:28,160 --> 00:24:29,880
I let him down.

455
00:24:33,720 --> 00:24:35,839
Used to putting on this act, aren't you?

456
00:24:38,519 --> 00:24:39,839
I really did let him down.

457
00:24:43,039 --> 00:24:44,079
Drop the act.

458
00:24:46,400 --> 00:24:48,000
Being able to use these people

459
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:50,160
who never even respected you...

460
00:24:50,279 --> 00:24:52,400
It feels pretty good, doesn't it?

461
00:24:53,480 --> 00:24:54,319
Why?

462
00:24:55,200 --> 00:24:56,160
Why

463
00:24:56,559 --> 00:24:59,039
can't you and I just talk normally?

464
00:25:00,119 --> 00:25:01,119
You might not believe this,

465
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:04,039
but because I treat you as my own

466
00:25:04,799 --> 00:25:07,160
that I'm so harsh to you.

467
00:25:07,279 --> 00:25:08,119
That's why I lose my temper with you.

468
00:25:08,119 --> 00:25:10,319
When can I see Yang Awu?

469
00:25:17,480 --> 00:25:18,799
Let's set the first rule.

470
00:25:19,119 --> 00:25:20,960
When I interrupt you,

471
00:25:21,359 --> 00:25:23,640
do not interrupt me.

472
00:25:25,240 --> 00:25:25,960
Okay?

473
00:25:39,880 --> 00:25:40,960
Actually,

474
00:25:42,119 --> 00:25:43,720
moving the trial date to next month

475
00:25:44,559 --> 00:25:46,000
takes just one phone call from me.

476
00:25:46,440 --> 00:25:48,279
I can do it without you breaking rules.

477
00:25:49,559 --> 00:25:51,599
Then why bother playing me?

478
00:25:51,680 --> 00:25:53,279
Because you're an interesting guy.

479
00:25:54,759 --> 00:25:55,480
You know what?

480
00:25:55,759 --> 00:25:58,119
I often observe you in private.

481
00:25:59,400 --> 00:26:02,359
I'll park by the road and watch you jog.

482
00:26:03,440 --> 00:26:04,559
Even at the courthouse.

483
00:26:04,759 --> 00:26:06,279
Seeing someone like you,

484
00:26:06,279 --> 00:26:07,720
so beloved,

485
00:26:08,640 --> 00:26:10,920
such a flawless, good person...

486
00:26:11,319 --> 00:26:13,480
I really can't get mad at you.

487
00:26:13,839 --> 00:26:15,119
But precisely because of that,

488
00:26:17,319 --> 00:26:19,119
I'm quite angry with you.

489
00:26:21,839 --> 00:26:23,559
Because I know about your son.

490
00:26:26,119 --> 00:26:27,960
I know who you truly are.

491
00:26:28,319 --> 00:26:29,160
Whenever you get a rape case,

492
00:26:29,160 --> 00:26:30,480
you love to give heavy sentences.

493
00:26:32,200 --> 00:26:34,039
You're trying to atone for your son.

494
00:26:34,880 --> 00:26:35,559
Right?

495
00:26:40,519 --> 00:26:42,200
I know you want to see Yang Awu.

496
00:26:44,359 --> 00:26:45,119
But right now,

497
00:26:45,119 --> 00:26:46,359
it's not that I won't let you see him.

498
00:26:47,960 --> 00:26:49,799
There's actually an obstacle.

499
00:26:49,960 --> 00:26:50,599
What?

500
00:26:51,960 --> 00:26:53,480
Know anyone at Rongshan County Court?

501
00:26:56,599 --> 00:26:58,960
What are you up to now?

502
00:27:01,160 --> 00:27:02,119
As for Yang Awu,

503
00:27:02,759 --> 00:27:03,720
he has an adoptive father.

504
00:27:04,680 --> 00:27:05,440
He's a hunter,

505
00:27:06,039 --> 00:27:07,079
and he has a hunting rifle.

506
00:27:08,119 --> 00:27:09,920
He refuses to hand the kid over.

507
00:27:10,960 --> 00:27:11,640
And I,

508
00:27:11,640 --> 00:27:12,920
have already hired local villagers

509
00:27:12,920 --> 00:27:14,720
to try and snatch the kid away.

510
00:27:15,240 --> 00:27:16,799
You've done so many terrible things.

511
00:27:18,359 --> 00:27:19,400
Aren't you afraid?

512
00:27:21,680 --> 00:27:22,759
Of course.

513
00:27:25,680 --> 00:27:27,160
After the villagers got hurt,

514
00:27:28,200 --> 00:27:31,319
I had someone go to the badly injured ones

515
00:27:31,519 --> 00:27:32,519
and give them compensation money.

516
00:27:33,480 --> 00:27:35,079
Think of it as hush money.

517
00:27:35,079 --> 00:27:36,119
Then I figured,

518
00:27:36,720 --> 00:27:37,599
if the hard way doesn't work,

519
00:27:37,599 --> 00:27:38,599
we'll do it the smart way.

520
00:27:39,240 --> 00:27:40,759
I have an anti-gang case.

521
00:27:41,440 --> 00:27:42,559
There's a client involved,

522
00:27:43,440 --> 00:27:44,200
and four years ago he...

523
00:27:44,200 --> 00:27:45,160
No, no, no.

524
00:27:46,680 --> 00:27:47,599
Stop right there.

525
00:27:47,920 --> 00:27:49,519
I won't help you with this.

526
00:27:52,559 --> 00:27:53,480
Don't even think about it.

527
00:27:54,079 --> 00:27:55,680
You've already guessed what I'm up to.

528
00:27:56,680 --> 00:27:58,319
Looks like I didn't misjudge you.

529
00:27:58,680 --> 00:27:59,960
You think exactly like I do.

530
00:28:00,400 --> 00:28:02,519
What you're doing is framing someone.

531
00:28:02,799 --> 00:28:04,039
Do you know that?

532
00:28:06,799 --> 00:28:07,599
I know.

533
00:28:08,799 --> 00:28:09,720
I had that person,

534
00:28:09,720 --> 00:28:11,359
while confessing for leniency,

535
00:28:11,440 --> 00:28:13,039
say Old Kang was also involved.

536
00:28:13,680 --> 00:28:14,839
Speaking of which, right now,

537
00:28:15,680 --> 00:28:17,000
our detective squad,

538
00:28:17,079 --> 00:28:19,319
with Rongshan County police's help,

539
00:28:19,920 --> 00:28:21,720
has already arrested Old Kang.

540
00:28:22,880 --> 00:28:24,519
The interrogation has been going on for days.

541
00:28:25,160 --> 00:28:27,839
Our Yang Awu is on a 3 PM flight,

542
00:28:28,079 --> 00:28:29,279
arriving at my house tonight.

543
00:28:29,759 --> 00:28:32,319
You are framing an innocent man right now.

544
00:28:34,680 --> 00:28:36,559
Think about it, if the police find out...

545
00:28:37,200 --> 00:28:38,039
we...

546
00:28:40,279 --> 00:28:41,039
"We."

547
00:28:42,519 --> 00:28:44,559
Looks like you're already on board.

548
00:28:53,079 --> 00:28:54,079
Don't worry.

549
00:28:55,319 --> 00:28:57,440
Due to the local geography

550
00:28:57,720 --> 00:28:59,160
and cultural issues,

551
00:28:59,680 --> 00:29:01,119
the loopholes in firearm registration

552
00:29:01,240 --> 00:29:02,519
have always been hard to fix.

553
00:29:02,559 --> 00:29:04,839
Plus, this is an old case from four years ago.

554
00:29:05,680 --> 00:29:07,279
We already have

555
00:29:07,279 --> 00:29:08,599
the confession of an accomplice.

556
00:29:08,799 --> 00:29:10,480
As long as Old Kang is willing to admit

557
00:29:10,480 --> 00:29:11,640
that the gun is his,

558
00:29:12,480 --> 00:29:14,039
the police will have enough evidence

559
00:29:14,039 --> 00:29:15,680
to transfer the case to the prosecutors.

560
00:29:16,119 --> 00:29:19,000
And for the prosecutors to file charges.

561
00:29:24,000 --> 00:29:25,000
This is absurd.

562
00:29:27,880 --> 00:29:29,240
You want his son,

563
00:29:29,240 --> 00:29:31,920
so you frame the father and get him arrested?

564
00:29:34,839 --> 00:29:36,519
Get your facts straight, will you?

565
00:29:37,480 --> 00:29:39,880
I am Yang Awu's father.

566
00:29:41,079 --> 00:29:43,599
I'm not in the mood for jokes.

567
00:29:47,400 --> 00:29:48,599
I don't want to either.

568
00:29:48,720 --> 00:29:50,400
As his adoptive father, Lao Kang

569
00:29:51,079 --> 00:29:53,400
went through a lot to raise Yang Awu.

570
00:29:53,599 --> 00:29:54,799
He raised him for four whole years.

571
00:29:56,599 --> 00:29:58,440
Anyone can understand his reluctance.

572
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:01,599
But right now, we don't have a plan

573
00:30:01,599 --> 00:30:03,319
to make him just let this go.

574
00:30:03,720 --> 00:30:04,559
Think about it.

575
00:30:05,599 --> 00:30:08,000
For every day this man is out there,

576
00:30:08,200 --> 00:30:09,000
you and I

577
00:30:09,880 --> 00:30:12,039
have to live in fear.

578
00:30:14,000 --> 00:30:18,480
Fine. Even if we put Lao Kang away,

579
00:30:18,599 --> 00:30:20,400
Yang Awu is already eight years old.

580
00:30:20,599 --> 00:30:21,720
How do we explain it to him?

581
00:30:21,759 --> 00:30:24,160
I'll find a lawyer from my firm

582
00:30:24,359 --> 00:30:25,880
to represent Lao Kang.

583
00:30:26,079 --> 00:30:28,400
He'll handle all of these matters for him.

584
00:30:28,400 --> 00:30:30,680
"Handle it" so you can control things.

585
00:30:30,960 --> 00:30:32,559
That doesn't matter.

586
00:30:32,680 --> 00:30:33,559
What's important is that,

587
00:30:34,240 --> 00:30:35,519
in the child's eyes,

588
00:30:36,079 --> 00:30:36,880
you and I

589
00:30:37,799 --> 00:30:40,440
are the great heroes saving Lao Kang.

590
00:30:43,000 --> 00:30:46,000
I can't keep this from the kid for the rest of my life.

591
00:30:46,720 --> 00:30:48,559
T-The rest of your life?

592
00:30:49,799 --> 00:30:51,960
You think you'll be that lucky?

593
00:30:51,960 --> 00:30:53,240
The rest of your life?

594
00:30:56,559 --> 00:30:58,880
Just hide it until you lose your memory.

595
00:31:00,519 --> 00:31:01,920
The rest of your life...

596
00:31:03,799 --> 00:31:04,839
Lao Yu,

597
00:31:06,720 --> 00:31:08,519
think about yourself instead.

598
00:31:14,839 --> 00:31:16,000
What I can guarantee

599
00:31:16,480 --> 00:31:19,559
is that Lao Kang's time in detention

600
00:31:19,759 --> 00:31:20,759
will be as long as possible.

601
00:31:22,359 --> 00:31:23,839
But once this case goes to court,

602
00:31:25,960 --> 00:31:28,039
how long he stays in prison...

603
00:31:29,920 --> 00:31:30,519
No,

604
00:31:31,039 --> 00:31:32,440
that will be up to you.

605
00:31:33,279 --> 00:31:36,200
This isn't just a rule violation anymore.

606
00:31:37,279 --> 00:31:41,160
Perjury is a crime!

607
00:31:44,799 --> 00:31:45,400
Fine.

608
00:31:46,799 --> 00:31:47,599
Everyone

609
00:31:48,440 --> 00:31:50,039
has the right to choose freely.

610
00:31:50,720 --> 00:31:52,720
You can go report me right now,

611
00:31:53,599 --> 00:31:54,480
save Lao Kang,

612
00:31:55,880 --> 00:31:58,200
and have all your son's scandals

613
00:31:58,680 --> 00:31:59,599
exposed to the public.

614
00:31:59,599 --> 00:32:01,400
Then you can go back to your

615
00:32:02,079 --> 00:32:03,400
empty house,

616
00:32:05,480 --> 00:32:06,880
and continue to be a

617
00:32:07,400 --> 00:32:09,039
boring,

618
00:32:10,119 --> 00:32:13,200
lonely pushover until you die.

619
00:32:20,880 --> 00:32:22,000
Or,

620
00:32:27,759 --> 00:32:29,640
try a different way of living.

621
00:32:33,359 --> 00:32:34,920
Be a little crazy.

622
00:32:38,000 --> 00:32:39,119
Make things interesting.

623
00:32:54,759 --> 00:32:55,720
As for tonight,

624
00:32:56,200 --> 00:32:57,160
just don't come over.

625
00:32:59,559 --> 00:33:02,559
We'll work together to eliminate risks,

626
00:33:03,880 --> 00:33:05,160
then arrange for you to meet.

627
00:33:08,240 --> 00:33:09,000
That's all.

628
00:33:10,039 --> 00:33:10,759
Thanks for your hard work.

629
00:33:27,839 --> 00:33:28,759
Dad wants you to go in.

630
00:33:45,079 --> 00:33:45,759
Dad

631
00:33:48,119 --> 00:33:48,799
Have a seat.

632
00:33:54,240 --> 00:33:55,359
All these years,

633
00:33:56,200 --> 00:33:57,599
what have you been so angry about?

634
00:34:00,160 --> 00:34:01,319
Your mother and I,

635
00:34:02,720 --> 00:34:04,000
and even young Director Fan,

636
00:34:05,359 --> 00:34:07,759
have walked on eggshells around you daily.

637
00:34:10,880 --> 00:34:12,159
We detectives

638
00:34:15,440 --> 00:34:18,199
work so hard to catch criminals,

639
00:34:19,559 --> 00:34:21,440
but you defense lawyers

640
00:34:22,599 --> 00:34:24,119
insist on setting them free.

641
00:34:24,840 --> 00:34:27,599
Insist on reducing their sentences.

642
00:34:28,599 --> 00:34:30,440
Insist on getting them less time.

643
00:34:31,119 --> 00:34:32,519
I just don't understand it.

644
00:34:33,880 --> 00:34:35,119
Is being a defense lawyer

645
00:34:35,119 --> 00:34:37,280
really a profession with a conscience?

646
00:34:38,679 --> 00:34:39,519
Is it honorable?

647
00:34:40,400 --> 00:34:41,480
Yet you insist on doing it.

648
00:34:44,039 --> 00:34:46,599
Why can't I ever get through to you?

649
00:34:48,480 --> 00:34:49,480
I'm old now.

650
00:34:50,400 --> 00:34:51,840
I've really tried my best.

651
00:35:00,119 --> 00:35:01,719
It's time to admit defeat.

652
00:35:07,679 --> 00:35:08,519
Ding Ning,

653
00:35:10,159 --> 00:35:12,000
I know you don't like me.

654
00:35:16,000 --> 00:35:17,639
I know you're afraid of me.

655
00:35:19,199 --> 00:35:21,039
But I'm afraid of you, too.

656
00:35:22,400 --> 00:35:24,320
I know you and Mom mean well,

657
00:35:25,559 --> 00:35:27,320
but when it comes to many people,

658
00:35:27,320 --> 00:35:29,119
many things, and many professions,

659
00:35:29,119 --> 00:35:30,440
our views are completely different.

660
00:35:31,199 --> 00:35:31,960
I have no way

661
00:35:31,960 --> 00:35:33,519
to explain it all clearly right now.

662
00:35:33,719 --> 00:35:34,480
But I don't...

663
00:35:34,480 --> 00:35:35,679
You follow the rules

664
00:35:38,559 --> 00:35:40,400
just to gather the strength

665
00:35:40,679 --> 00:35:41,880
to resist the rules.

666
00:35:43,280 --> 00:35:44,760
You act submissive

667
00:35:47,920 --> 00:35:49,400
and pretend to love us.

668
00:36:16,719 --> 00:36:17,400
Dad.

669
00:36:20,840 --> 00:36:21,639
Maybe...

670
00:36:24,239 --> 00:36:26,079
I should move out for now.

671
00:36:50,960 --> 00:36:52,159
Hey, Mom.

672
00:36:52,159 --> 00:36:53,639
So you're running away from home now?

673
00:36:54,039 --> 00:36:55,360
Fine. You're all grown up.

674
00:36:55,360 --> 00:36:56,519
You've got your wings now.

675
00:36:58,039 --> 00:36:58,880
Oh, right.

676
00:36:59,039 --> 00:37:00,559
We don't have cash at home.

677
00:37:00,559 --> 00:37:01,679
It's all in fixed deposits.

678
00:37:01,679 --> 00:37:02,639
So for your dad's medical bills,

679
00:37:02,639 --> 00:37:04,400
I took the money from your card.

680
00:37:04,800 --> 00:37:05,440
Also,

681
00:37:05,440 --> 00:37:07,079
the other day at Aunt Wang's,

682
00:37:07,079 --> 00:37:08,280
I bought an insurance policy for you.

683
00:37:08,280 --> 00:37:09,039
Remember?

684
00:37:09,039 --> 00:37:10,239
I already agreed to it.

685
00:37:10,239 --> 00:37:11,079
The contract is already signed.

686
00:37:11,079 --> 00:37:12,000
It can't be canceled.

687
00:37:12,000 --> 00:37:13,320
You'll have to pay the premiums yourself.

688
00:37:14,760 --> 00:37:15,440
Are you listening?

689
00:37:15,719 --> 00:37:17,639
Did you hear me? Say something!

690
00:37:18,079 --> 00:37:18,679
Fine.

691
00:37:59,639 --> 00:38:02,199
They're tearing down this bridge. Did you know?

692
00:38:15,480 --> 00:38:16,320
I saw it.

693
00:38:17,000 --> 00:38:18,639
It's so late. Are you okay?

694
00:38:21,639 --> 00:38:23,639
Even if it brings back memories for many,

695
00:38:24,320 --> 00:38:25,920
it will still be torn down and erased.

696
00:38:26,960 --> 00:38:28,840
Because everyone just wants to move forward.

697
00:38:29,719 --> 00:38:33,000
Only you and I willingly live in the past.

698
00:38:48,800 --> 00:38:50,000
Let's meet up.

699
00:38:51,960 --> 00:38:53,039
Okay.

700
00:38:53,800 --> 00:38:55,320
I'll treat you to a late-night snack.

701
00:38:56,840 --> 00:38:57,559
Yijie.

702
00:38:58,760 --> 00:39:00,559
The final candidate for Old Kang's case...

703
00:39:02,599 --> 00:39:03,480
I recommend him.

704
00:39:04,239 --> 00:39:05,199
Zhou Hao.

705
00:39:05,199 --> 00:39:06,880
Yes. He's quite impressionable.

706
00:39:07,119 --> 00:39:08,679
He's been at our firm under two months.

707
00:39:08,760 --> 00:39:10,480
He's eager to prove himself.

708
00:39:10,480 --> 00:39:12,320
Most importantly, his employment records

709
00:39:12,320 --> 00:39:13,679
haven't been fully transferred over.

710
00:39:13,679 --> 00:39:14,760
If something goes wrong,

711
00:39:15,239 --> 00:39:16,159
we can easily wash our hands of him.

712
00:39:18,360 --> 00:39:19,719
What about his social connections?

713
00:39:20,000 --> 00:39:20,719
His father

714
00:39:20,719 --> 00:39:21,960
is a university law professor.

715
00:39:22,039 --> 00:39:24,119
His mother is a successful businesswoman.

716
00:39:24,159 --> 00:39:25,559
Do you know what this kid

717
00:39:25,719 --> 00:39:27,840
chose to do first after college?

718
00:39:28,079 --> 00:39:29,760
He insisted on joining Changyu Law Firm.

719
00:39:31,079 --> 00:39:31,760
Is that so?

720
00:39:33,280 --> 00:39:34,239
That's just perfect.

721
00:39:35,559 --> 00:39:37,079
Kids like him are the easiest to mold.

722
00:39:37,599 --> 00:39:39,559
Alright, he's the one.

723
00:39:40,079 --> 00:39:41,719
Arrange for them to sign the contract right away.

724
00:39:41,960 --> 00:39:42,639
Okay.

725
00:39:46,599 --> 00:39:47,360
Slow down.

726
00:39:47,440 --> 00:39:48,840
What's wrong? Wasn't he taking a bath?

727
00:39:50,079 --> 00:39:51,360
This kid is too stubborn.

728
00:39:51,519 --> 00:39:52,960
He refuses to undress for a bath.

729
00:39:53,960 --> 00:39:54,679
Mr. Zhao,

730
00:39:55,039 --> 00:39:56,000
from now on, after work,

731
00:39:56,000 --> 00:39:57,000
for things like bathing the kid,

732
00:39:57,000 --> 00:39:58,119
please don't call me.

733
00:39:58,440 --> 00:39:59,719
Sorry. I'm sorry.

734
00:40:03,880 --> 00:40:05,519
Alright, I'll leave you to it.

735
00:40:06,159 --> 00:40:06,880
I'm heading out too.

736
00:40:11,719 --> 00:40:12,719
You should get some rest too, Auntie.

737
00:40:13,119 --> 00:40:14,039
I'll handle it myself.

738
00:40:14,079 --> 00:40:14,760
Okay.

739
00:40:50,000 --> 00:40:52,039
I know your Chinese isn't great.

740
00:40:53,280 --> 00:40:55,400
But you can understand me, right?

741
00:41:00,320 --> 00:41:01,920
I can save your dad.

742
00:41:05,840 --> 00:41:06,440
Dad?

743
00:41:06,440 --> 00:41:07,079
Yes.

744
00:41:10,280 --> 00:41:11,679
So you need to listen to me.

745
00:41:12,800 --> 00:41:14,599
No more messing around like this.

746
00:41:15,519 --> 00:41:16,239
Okay?

747
00:41:21,239 --> 00:41:23,559
Do you want to stay in here tonight?

748
00:41:31,239 --> 00:41:31,840
Fine.

749
00:41:41,639 --> 00:41:42,400
Good night.

750
00:41:59,760 --> 00:42:01,239
Is this enough?

751
00:42:01,719 --> 00:42:04,280
Should we order something more filling? Rice?

752
00:42:04,280 --> 00:42:05,360
No need. This is plenty.

753
00:42:07,599 --> 00:42:08,519
How are you holding up?

754
00:42:14,800 --> 00:42:16,880
I thought my world would fall apart.

755
00:42:18,039 --> 00:42:18,920
But actually...

756
00:42:21,159 --> 00:42:23,400
I guess this outcome feels more real.

757
00:42:25,320 --> 00:42:27,840
You actually feel more at peace, right?

758
00:42:38,559 --> 00:42:39,519
Hello, Mr. Ye.

759
00:42:44,440 --> 00:42:45,079
What?

760
00:42:46,519 --> 00:42:47,679
Lao Kang was taken away?

761
00:42:48,920 --> 00:42:50,320
Slow down.

762
00:42:50,719 --> 00:42:51,679
What about Yang Awu?

763
00:42:52,880 --> 00:42:53,559
Okay, I got it.

764
00:42:55,719 --> 00:42:56,360
What happened?

765
00:42:57,679 --> 00:42:59,519
I met a little boy in the mountains.

766
00:43:00,199 --> 00:43:02,639
A boy who could barely speak Mandarin.

767
00:43:02,639 --> 00:43:03,920
An ethnic minority boy.
